// State pix (f_tf_smooth): the temporal one-pole recurrence, per channel, in
// tensor space. in1 = this frame's raw tensor (f_tensor_type.md outlet-0
// encoding, unchanged by smoothing); in2 = previous frame's blended output
// (feedback loop, see codebox_render.gen + definition.py pix_wires).
// Mirrors tests/test_tf_smooth.py smooth_step exactly.
//
//   T' = T_new + release * (T_prev - T_new)
//
// ADR-3: NO clamp anywhere. Raw tensor values are unbounded floats (strong
// edges give Jxx*strength >> 1); clipping inside a feedback loop creates
// stuck-at-boundary artifacts. The outlet encoding IS the inlet encoding
// (raw tensor passthrough), so this module never encodes or clamps at all.
// No decode, no atan2: this codebox is 4-channel arithmetic only.
//
// ADR-4: bypass_gate (module bypass, bypass_mode "param"; NOT the native
// @bypass, which would skip the shader and flip feedback semantics) is an
// exact passthrough with the feedback IGNORED -- not a freeze of the last
// smoothed frame. On an unconnected inlet (vs_black = zero tensor) the
// feedback decays naturally to the zero-tensor neutral instead of holding a
// stale field.
//
// GATE PROVISIONAL-OPEN (spec OQ1 / tasks T016): release default 0.5 and the
// dial ceiling are PROVISIONAL, pending tier-3 judgement on live noise.
// The shipped literal follows definition.py's declared default (0.5).
Param release(0.5);
Param bypass_gate(0.0);

new_t = sample(in1, norm);            // inline access (stored-variable .x silent-fails)
prev_t = sample(in2, norm);

// Per-channel one-pole. mix(a, b, w) = a + w*(b - a): blend(prev, new, 1-release)
// = new + release*(prev - new) with no float32 reorder surprises.
out1 = mix(prev_t, new_t, -release + 1.0);
// ADR-4 bypass: passthrough of the inlet, feedback ignored.
out1 = mix(out1, new_t, bypass_gate);